# deny.patterns.example
#
# Patterns in this file are ALWAYS BLOCKED — no user prompt, just denied.
# Copy this file to ~/.clawband/deny.patterns and edit to customise.
#
# Format:
#   - One pattern per line
#   - Case-insensitive extended regex (grep -iE)
#   - Lines starting with # and blank lines are ignored
#   - These patterns are ADDED to the built-in deny list, not a replacement
#
# To suppress a built-in block, add the pattern to allow.patterns instead.
#
# ── Examples ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Block a project-specific destruction command
# my-infra nuke --all

# Block a custom deploy script from running without confirmation (use ask.patterns for prompt instead)
# deploy-prod.sh

# Block access to a sensitive directory
# rm.*secrets/

# Block any docker system prune
# docker system prune
